## Overview

Follow-up to #64509 and #67393. Extend the Qwen3.5 NVIDIA fused output-gate paths (`fused_gdn_gated_rms_norm` → `out_proj` and `fused_sigmoid_gate_mul` → `o_proj`) from static FP8 (`kFp8StaticTensorSym`) to dynamic per-token FP8 (`kFp8DynamicTokenSym`), removing the remaining 64 standalone `dynamic_per_token_scaled_fp8_quant` launches and BF16 HBM round-trips per forward pass on a 64-layer Qwen3.5-27B model (48 GDN + 16 full-attention layers).

Not a duplicate: #64509 fused static FP8 only on these two producers; #67393 extended `gemma_add_rms_norm_quant` to dynamic per-token FP8;

## Motivation

On MI355X (gfx950), the decode/verify prologue of each Kimi-K3.1 DSA attention layer is a chain of small launches:

- separate GEMMs for `fused_qkv_a`, the indexer's `wk` and `weights_proj`, and the output gate's `g_proj`;
- the index-key LayerNorm, index-K store, query quant and head gate as separate ops;
- a separate FP8 quant and store for the `fp8_ds_mla` KV cache.

At low and medium batch sizes, these launches and the extra activation round trips are a noticeable share of step time. vLLM fuses this prologue in vllm-project/vllm#67847. This PR brings the same fusion to SGLan

